  "worked_solution": "Notice that the function $h(x)$ is differentiable for all $x\\ne 1.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $h(x)=\\frac{1}{x-1}.$\n\nThe other functions are not differentiable at $x=-1.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ has a vertical tangent at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is not defined at $x=-1$ and hence it is not differentiable there.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
